<%# `Media::PickerComponent`'s grid (round 3, Task 9): `Admin::MediaController#index`
    with `picker=1`, rendered without a layout into the picker's own
    `<turbo-frame id="media-picker-grid">` -- the toolbar's form and the page links
    below stay inside that frame (Turbo scopes a frame's own forms and links to it),
    so searching, choosing a segment and paging never navigate the editor underneath
    the modal, and the dialog never closes or jumps. `picker` rides along in the
    toolbar's form (hidden field) and in the pagination links (`list_params`, which
    names it among the keys to keep), so every later request comes back here, not to
    the full Media module page. The toolbar is the Media screen's own
    (`Admin::MediaLibrary::ToolbarComponent`, `picker: true`), the tiles the grid's
    (`pick: true`). %>
<turbo-frame id="media-picker-grid">
  <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::ToolbarComponent.new(counts: @counts, filter: @search.filter, q: params[:q], url_options: admin_url_options, picker: true) %>

  <% page_url = ->(page) { admin_media_path(list_params(:q, :filter, :picker).merge("page" => page)) } %>
  <% if @pagination.out_of_range? %>
    <%= render "admin/shared/out_of_range_page", url: page_url.call(1) %>
  <% else %>
    <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::GridComponent.new(assets: @assets, url_options: admin_url_options, pick: true, locale: admin_locale) %>
    <% if @pagination.total_pages > 1 %>
      <div class="mt-4 rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface">
        <%= render Admin::PaginationComponent.new(pagination: @pagination, url: page_url) %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</turbo-frame>
